SUMMARY:Bent Creek: Green’s Lick to Stradley Mountain –8miles\, 1350
 ’ ascent
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**NOTE EARLIER START TIME DUE TO T
 HE HEAT!**\n**Place to Meet: Bent Creek River Park** 1592 Brevard Rd (appr
 ox. 1/10 mile south of the Arboretum on Hwy 191). driving from there to th
 e trailhead: Campground Connector in Bent Creek--limited parking\; don't d
 rive directly to the trailhead. Departing on time---8:30. Look for Silver 
 Lincoln SUV Mark Montgomery cell #239-777-4743\n**Description\;** Hike thr
 ough Bent Creek to Four Points on Stradley Mountain. Good footing\; mostly
  wide trails\; nearby creeks\, but no panoramic views. Ascending via Lower
  Sidehill and Green’s Lick. Descending via Little Hickory with a snack b
 reak at the picnic tables on Boyd Branch. Type: loop. Max elev: 3300’. A
 vg moving pace: 2.4 mph. Difficulty (1=effortless\, 10=hard): 5.5. Dogs: w
 elcome if well-behaved and leashed\, subject to area restrictions.\n**As u
 sual\, there will be opportunity to have lunch and/or a beverage after the
  hike at the Stoneridge Tavern.**\n\n\\*\\***Courtesy** (Please read caref
 ully!)\\*\\* Only sign up if you \\\\\\*truly\\\\\\* plan to come. If you 
 must cancel\, please change your status to "Not Going" as soon as possible
 . Avoid dropping out within 24 hours of the hike so that wait-listers can 
 have sufficient notice. And please please PLEASE don't be a no-show\n\n**L
 EGALESE**\nThis Asheville Hiking Group event involves hiking and\, possibl
 y\, transportation to and from the meetup site. Participants are responsib
 le for their own safety and affirm that they have the appropriate skills\,
  physical conditioning\, equipment\, and supplies. Hiking may involve risk
 s to oneself and property. Neither your hike organizer nor Asheville Hikin
 g Group can assure your safety nor eliminate all risks. Participants assum
 e full responsibility for any injuries\, damages\, or losses.
