SUMMARY:Graybeard Falls -- 6 mi\, 1\,200 ft. gain
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**[Sign-up opens Sunday\, Aug. 9th
  at 8 PM]**\n\nThe Mt. Graybeard Trail is a favorite of many\, myself incl
 uded. We’ll do an out-and-back\, around 3.1 miles up\, then the same com
 ing back. There's a clearing by Graybeard Falls where we'll take a little 
 break before heading down.\n\nThis is not an easy hike! Because of the lon
 g uphill segment and lots of heads-down walking over roots & rocks\, I’m
  giving this a solid 5.0 difficulty level on a 10-point scale. We'll move 
 at a fairly good pace\, averaging around 2.3 mph. If you're a first-timer 
 and unsure if you're good with 1\,000'+ elevation gains\, it's best not to
  attend this one and risk holding back the group.\n\nIf you ever use hikin
 g poles\, they'd be useful here. Prepare for a trio of stream crossings wi
 th some potential rock-hopping depending on water levels. The trail can be
  muddy in parts\, too. Yes\, this hike can be a bit sloppy\, but it's wort
 h it!\n\nWear good hiking shoes\, bring some water\, and a little snack if
  so inclined.\n\n***Dog Policy:*** Dogs are welcome but must be leashed.\n
 \n***Guest Policy:*** If you'd like to bring a guest\, they'll need to joi
 n the Asheville Hiking Group and sign up for the hike on their own. Altern
 atively\, if you've made it onto the "Going" list\, contact me in advance 
 and ask if it's okay to bring a "+1". Depending on timing and demand\, I m
 ay be able to add your guest.\n\n**MEET-UP TIME & PLACE**\n\nParking at th
 e trailhead is very tight\, so carpooling is a must. Let's meet promptly b
 y **9:00 AM** at the **Black Mountain Ingles at 550 Route NC-9. It's near 
 Exit 64 off I-40**. We’ll gather at the **north end** of the Ingles park
 ing lot toward McDonald's (but not in the McD's lot)\, which is toward the
  right when you enter the Ingles lot. Look for my car\, a silver Hyundai s
 edan.\n\nOn Google Maps: **[https://bit.ly/3TLR4yG](https://bit.ly/3TLR4yG
 )**\n\nWe'll organize into as few vehicles as possible\, then drive the 15
  minutes to the Graybeard Trailhead.\n\n**COURTESY TO WAIT-LISTERS**\nOnly
  sign up if you definitely plan to come. If you must cancel\, please chang
 e your status to "Not Going" as soon as possible so wait-listers can have 
 sufficient notice. And please please PLEASE don't be a no-show.\n\nIf you'
 re on the waiting list\, keep checking through the evening before the hike
 . We often get last-minute dropouts. Also\, if you know at some point that
  you won't be able to attend even if someone drops out\, please remove you
 rself from the waiting list.\n\n**WEATHER**\nI'll watch the weather and po
 st a cancellation message by 7:30 AM if the forecast is >50% chance of pre
 cipitation.\n\n**QUESTIONS?**\nYou can message me through MeetUp until 8:0
 0 AM the day of. Cell reception may be sketchy\, but you can try to text o
 r call me up to the start of the hike: (803) 767-3094.\n\n**LEGALESE**\nTh
 is Asheville Hiking Group event involves hiking and\, possibly\, transport
 ation to and from the meetup site. Participants are responsible for their 
 own safety and affirm that they have the appropriate skills\, physical con
 ditioning\, equipment\, and supplies. Hiking may involve risks to oneself 
 and property. Neither your hike organizer nor Asheville Hiking Group can a
 ssure your safety nor eliminate all risks. Participants assume full respon
 sibility for any injuries\, damages\, or losses.
